What this solution actually does: a timer-driven Windows Service obtains pending customer FIEL values from TOMI, checks schedules/business-day state, sends SOAP certificate-query/validation requests to a configured SPID endpoint, interprets response values, and persists status/result information. It also updates service execution state and creates operational alerts. There is no inbound web/API host, message-queue listener, or demonstrated local private-key/signing implementation in this repository.
The executable is currently under the nested SPID_FIEL directory, not the historical Entradas host path. See the understanding document (../excecutive_docs/SPID_FIEL/Application_understanding_technical_document.md) and verified dependency ladder (../excecutive_docs/SPID_FIEL/Base_Project_Dependency_Ladder.md).
