{
    // Processing.
}
finally
{
    await _IparametrosOperaciones.MarcarServicioEnFinalizacion(_configuracion.NombreServicio);
}
Once execution has been marked, parameter retrieval/parsing, required-key validation, business-day lookup, or the out-of-hours alert can fail before the try is entered. The tick's finalization is then skipped. The host logging the error or clearing state at eventual service shutdown does not repair that failed tick.
Fix: put all post-marking work inside the protected region, preserving the original failure if cleanup also fails:
Code block (csharp)
await _IparametrosOperaciones.MarcarServicioEnEjecucion(_configuracion.NombreServicio);
try
{
    await LoadValidateAndProcessTickAsync();
}
finally
{
    await FinalizeTickAndReportCleanupOutcomeAsync();
}
The two helper names illustrate extraction of existing work; they must be implemented with explicit primary/cleanup error reporting and the checked-result policy in FIEL-FR-4, not silent catches.
Benefit / tests: execution state does not remain active after malformed/missing parameters or alert failure. Inject failures at parameter load, each validation boundary, alerting, processing, and cleanup; assert finalization is attempted once after a successful mark and primary/cleanup failures remain observable.
