Check the token between records, preserve OperationCanceledException, and retain the host's separate cleanup token. Merely passing a token to Task.Run does not cancel an already-running synchronous request.
Benefit / tests: a stop during connection, response-body read, or a multi-FIEL batch promptly stops further processing; no new record is processed after cancellation, and cleanup behavior is verified without live services.
