The known workload is a timer-driven sequential read/query/update integration worker. It already has layered projects, constructor injection and a central Windows-service lifecycle. There is no demonstrated inbound API, durable queue trigger, scaling bottleneck, or multi-step financial saga that would by itself justify microservices or a workflow engine.
